# {{ display_name }} Deploy Integration

## Overview
{% if category in ('ai-ml',) %}
Deploy {{ display_name }}-powered applications as stateless API wrappers — serverless functions
that receive user requests, call the {{ display_name }} model API, and stream responses back.
{% elif category in ('data-platform',) %}
Deploy {{ display_name }} integrations as data pipeline workers — persistent services that
maintain database connections, run scheduled queries, and process data continuously.
{% elif category in ('developer-tools',) %}
Deploy using {{ display_name }}'s native deployment tools. Configuration lives in the
project repo and deploys trigger via git push or CLI commands.
{% elif category in ('sales-crm', 'communication') %}
Deploy {{ display_name }} integrations as webhook workers — always-on endpoints that
receive events (contact created, message sent) and trigger downstream actions.
{% elif category in ('design-creative',) %}
Deploy {{ display_name }} integration as a CI/CD pipeline step that exports assets,
syncs design tokens, or generates code from design files during the build.
{% elif category in ('fintech',) %}
Deploy {{ display_name }} integrations as secure webhook workers with HMAC signature
verification, idempotent processing, and dead-letter queues for reliability.
{% elif category in ('infra-ops',) %}
Deploy {{ display_name }} as a sidecar agent alongside your application, plus webhook
endpoints for alert routing and incident response automation.
{% else %}
Deploy {{ display_name }}-powered applications to popular platforms with proper secrets management.
{% endif %}

## Prerequisites
- {{ display_name }} API keys for production environment
- Platform CLI installed (vercel, fly, or gcloud)
- Application code ready for deployment
